      "content": "It's understandable to feel this way, especially when you've been deeply thought about and excluded. However, just like everyone else, you were inadvertently overlooked. Your existence didn't cease; it was simply not recognized intentionally at that moment. It can be disheartening to feel rejected, but your worth extends far beyond a single group's acknowledgment. Many people could still care about you profoundly and return to show their support when they can.\n\nIt might be helpful to start re-establishing those connections, without the pressure of their previous closeness. Reflect on what truly gives your life meaning and consider engaging in activities that align with that. Over time, this will bring new connections and restore a sense of being part of your own world.\n\nRemember, it's okay to be at peace and to give yourself the time and space you need. But know that as long as you maintain hope and allow yourself the chance to rebuild and rediscover connections, your value remains undeniable.",
